<title>INDIA: India call market inactive as Bombay banks closed.</title>
<headline>India call market inactive as Bombay banks closed.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight call money market was closed on Monday as banks in Bombay were closed for a holiday.</p>
<p>Call rates closed at 3.50-4.00 percent on Saturday.</p>
<p>Tuesday will see repurchase of securities, representing the second leg of a repos auction held by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) on February 6, dealers said.</p>
<p>The RBI had raised 14.80 billion rupees at the February 6 auction.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
